WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.905
Application security matters for SaaS and cloud environments because customers trust hosted systems with sensitive data, workflows, integrations, and identity information.

2
00:00:10.905 --> 00:00:19.646
A weakness in an application can become a direct risk to confidentiality, availability, processing integrity, or customer trust.

3
00:00:19.646 --> 00:00:23.458
OWASP provides community-driven application security guidance.

4
00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:33.385
The OWASP Top 10 gives development, DevSecOps, security, and compliance teams a common language for discussing the most important web application risks.

5
00:00:33.385 --> 00:00:38.464
SOC 2 reports evaluate controls against Trust Services Criteria.

6
00:00:38.464 --> 00:00:50.826
The Security category is required for SOC 2 and focuses on protecting systems and data through logical access, system operations, change management, risk mitigation, and monitoring.

7
00:00:50.826 --> 00:00:57.970
Application security supports SOC 2 by making controls practical inside the software delivery lifecycle.

8
00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:06.980
Secure coding, access control, monitoring, vulnerability management, and change management all produce the operational evidence auditors expect.

9
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:16.119
Each module explains an OWASP risk, practical attack examples, mitigations, and selected SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria mappings.

10
00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:22.475
The mappings support awareness and planning, but they do not replace formal audit scoping or control testing.

11
00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:26.018
Use OWASP categories to organize application risk work.

12
00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:31.226
Use SOC 2 criteria to connect technical safeguards to control objectives.

13
00:01:31.226 --> 00:01:36.444
Validate mappings with the organization's security, compliance, and audit stakeholders.

14
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:40.495
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC3.

15
00:01:40.495 --> 00:01:43.299
2 - Risk identification; CC7.

16
00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:46.223
1 - Vulnerability management; CC8.

17
00:01:46.223 --> 00:01:48.069
1 - Change management processes.
